<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiménez dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/905">905</a>–<a href="/years/1234">1234</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Jimena dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jiménez dynasty ruled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, from 905, when Sancho Garcés I took the throne, until 1234. Its greatest king, Sancho III, dominated Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in the early 11th century, and his sons founded the royal lines of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and Aragon. After the death of Sancho VII in 1234, Navarre passed to the counts of Champagne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jimenez-dynasty.jpg" alt="Jiménez dynasty" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armas_de_la_Dinastia_Jimena_de_Navarra.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
